# Git: land on develop

This repo's integration branch is `develop`. `main` is release-only.

At the start of any session that will edit files:

1. If `HEAD` is `main`, detached, or a leftover `codex/*` branch, check out `develop` immediately (`git checkout develop` or `git checkout -B develop origin/develop`).
2. Fast-forward `develop` from `origin/develop` when behind. Do not rebase onto `main` as a working branch.
3. Call `SetActiveBranch` with `develop`.

Never commit, amend, or push to `main`. Never recreate `codex/windows-integration` or other Codex integration branches. Open PRs from `develop` to `main` only when a slice is ready to publish.

If you find yourself on `main` with a dirty tree, move to `develop` before more edits. Preserve unrelated changes.
